      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Solve $x^2 - 5x + 6 > 0$.",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$2 < x < 3$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$x < 2$ or $x > 3$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$x > 6$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$x < -2$ or $x > -3$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Factorise: $(x-2)(x-3) > 0$. The roots are $x = 2$ and $x = 3$. Since the quadratic is positive (opens upward), it is greater than zero outside the roots: $x < 2$ or $x > 3$."
